{"qualification-report.md": "# Unchanged-Source online backup fixture qualification\n\nDate: 2026-10-15. Scope: `online-backup-fixture-qualification-scope.json` SHA-256 `5ce1dd8bea33a4205a2e357b4ca2364b41505a077fab9d2deb64b053fa65ea22`. Pinned detached Source HEAD `4f4023c956f84d65743f39ce77d6c8899a21ada1`, tree `3db13a15cc52b2b0bd75cae3452c66509a9f55c9`; final `git status --porcelain=v1` empty. No tracked Source edit. This is isolated fixture qualification only: actual backup authority 0, formal acceptance increment 0, self-acceptance false.\n\n## Result\n\n| Case | Controlled fixture result | Boundary |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Q01, no active workspace | PASS for the finite two-process fixture: real pinned `ops/backup` CLI create and `restore --as-data-root` exited 0; restored SQLite integrity `ok`; all 88 source tables, schema and migration census equal before/after create. | No active workspace. Restored `auth_credentials` differs because restore bootstraps a fresh owner. |\n| Q02, real Host-authorized workspace | PASS for the finite two-process fixture: CLI create and operational restore exited 0; small file SHA-256 `c9f09e0a76fbbf83847013f7d79aa09c1566778489cc499e76e3e5d72b1c8db6` and empty directory restored; active binding kept authorized ref/project and moved under the new restored root. SQLite integrity `ok`; all 88 source tables, schema and migration census equal before/after create. | Restored `Project.real_path` and `Project.revision` change by rebinding; `auth_credentials` changes by new owner. No original/live workspace was touched. |\n| Q03, Run with UNKNOWN effect and client queue | PASS for the finite current-schema fixture: current pinned schema migration 24/88 tables, real unchanged CLI create and operational restore exit 0; source 88 tables/schema equal before and after create; restore reports `RESTORED_RECONCILIATION_REQUIRED`, `external_actions_dispatched=0`. | Run/effect were made by current public orchestration and effect APIs with zero external dispatch. Queue was made by `goalCommand`; one UNKNOWN phase and a revoked workspace binding were seeded by explicitly fixture-only SQL plus the existing receipt helper. The production queue validator and CLI backup validators passed. This does **not** establish that a real worker/provider produced the historical facts. |\n\nFor Q01–Q03, a separate process held `adapters/runtime.AcquireDataRootLease` on the same fixture data root throughout create. An independent process acquire probe exited 10 before and after create, then exited 0 after holder's normal exit; holder native exit was 0. The real CLI's create and restore exits were 0. The initialized baseline was taken before create. Readable source file hashes and native ACL snapshots remained unchanged; WAL/SHM mtime changed without hash changes. A separate repeat `Host.New` check after Q02 also left all 88 tables, schema and native ACL unchanged, with only WAL/SHM mtime changes. See `run-q01-r2.*`, `run-q02.*`, `run-q03-current-r2.*`, `compare-q01-r2.stdout.raw`, `compare-q02.stdout.raw`, `compare-q03-current.stdout.raw`, `compare-q02-repeat-host.stdout.raw`, and per-command `*.recipe.json`/`*.exit.json`/raw output.\n\nQ03 source Run is `QUEUED`, effect history has one `UNKNOWN`, queue has one `UNKNOWN`, control request is `REQUESTED`, and binding is `REVOKED`. After restore, Run is `RECONCILING`; the original UNKNOWN effect remains and restore appends an UNKNOWN reconciliation record; queue UNKNOWN persists; control request is `RECONCILING`; binding remains REVOKED. The restore adds an audit barrier and receipt. `verify-q03-current-history-r5.stdout.raw` and `read-q03-restored-report.stdout.raw` record those states. Its native ACL snapshot is equal before/after create, and restored differences are limited to the 12 explicitly recorded restore-related tables; immutable content tables are unchanged. The copied old controlled candidate was independently inspected: migration 22/84 tables and active binding outside this task root. It was not migrated or used for this current-schema result; see `inspect-q03-candidate-r3.stdout.raw`. The first Q03 builder failed on a goal/task problem-id mismatch; its database remains as diagnostic. The corrected builder and CLI fixture used a separate `current-data-r2` root.\n\nQ02 refusal cuts each used the real CLI. Existing destination exited 1 with `DESTINATION_EXISTS` and original encrypted package file census unchanged. Wrong recovery key exited 1 with `BACKUP_MANIFEST_INVALID` and published root absent. A changed workspace root identity, despite identical visible file contents, exited 1 with `BACKUP_WORKSPACE_PIN_CHANGED` and published package absent. See `verify-negative-cuts.stdout.raw`, the three `q02-refuse-*` / `q02-wrong-key-restore` command records, and package censuses. Q01 and Q02 native ACL snapshot equality is recorded in `verify-negative-cuts.stdout.raw`.\n\nThe encrypted packages remain in the task temporary fixture root for independent replay. Recovery key files remain separately in its private key directory; key bytes were never copied into receipt outputs. The task root and key directory were ACL-restricted to the current user; the initial task-root ACL command failed due to a SID formatting error and its exit was retained before the corrected retry. Build/cache/fixture files are retained only because they are needed to replay the frozen proof; no original `.local` data, original Host API, original keys, worker, model or provider was accessed. The initial Q01 observation failed while trying to read an exclusively locked `coordinator.lock`; the corrected file census marks that lock as unreadable, and Q01 r2 passed. Diagnostic attempts remain in the ledger, not deleted.\n\nAn idle held lease establishes online create while another process owns the root lease. It does not establish a snapshot under arbitrary concurrent business writes. SQLite documents `VACUUM INTO` as a consistent snapshot, WAL reader/writer concurrency, and transaction isolation: [VACUUM INTO](https://www.sqlite.org/lang_vacuum.html), [WAL](https://www.sqlite.org/wal.html), [isolation](https://sqlite.org/isolation.html). A controlled atomic writer and point-in-time assertion remain untested here. This is a fixture boundary for independent review, not a live provider qualification.\n\nThe original root's workspace census, source size/limits, recovery key, Host initialization side effects, and restore credentials remain unknown. No actual-root permission was granted. Root must independently review this evidence and qualify those resources before an actual backup plan; this worker issues no acceptance.\n", "qualification-report.json": {"schema": "researchos.online-backup-fixture-qualification.v1", "source_commit": "4f4023c956f84d65743f39ce77d6c8899a21ada1", "source_tree": "3db13a15cc52b2b0bd75cae3452c66509a9f55c9", "scope_sha256": "5ce1dd8bea33a4205a2e357b4ca2364b41505a077fab9d2deb64b053fa65ea22", "actual_backup_authority": false, "formal_acceptance_increment": 0, "self_acceptance": false, "cases": {"Q01": {"status": "FINITE_FIXTURE_PASS", "run": "run-q01-r2", "source_census": "compare-q01-r2.stdout.raw", "restore": "verify-q01-r2-restore.stdout.raw"}, "Q02": {"status": "FINITE_FIXTURE_PASS", "run": "run-q02", "source_census": "compare-q02.stdout.raw", "restore": "verify-q02-restore-r2.stdout.raw", "negative_cuts": "verify-negative-cuts.stdout.raw"}, "Q03": {"status": "FINITE_FIXTURE_PASS", "run": "run-q03-current-r2", "builder": "q03-build-current-fixture-r2", "source_census": "compare-q03-current.stdout.raw", "restore": "verify-q03-current-history-r5.stdout.raw", "fixture_only_sql": ["UNKNOWN client_command_queue receipt/state", "REVOKED workspace binding"], "public_api": ["goalCommand", "PrepareEffect", "BeginEffect", "ObserveEffect UNKNOWN"], "old_candidate_excluded": "inspect-q03-candidate-r3.stdout.raw"}}, "remaining_limit": "No controlled concurrent business writer point-in-time assertion; idle held lease only."}, "Q01-Q03-cuts-matrix.json": {"Q01": {"lease_probe_before": 10, "create": 0, "lease_probe_after": 10, "lease_probe_after_release": 0, "restore": 0, "source_all_tables_equal": true}, "Q02": {"lease_probe_before": 10, "create": 0, "lease_probe_after": 10, "lease_probe_after_release": 0, "restore": 0, "source_all_tables_equal": true}, "Q03": {"lease_probe_before": 10, "create": 0, "lease_probe_after": 10, "lease_probe_after_release": 0, "restore": 0, "source_all_tables_equal": true, "history_assertions": "verify-q03-current-history-r5.stdout.raw"}, "cuts": {"changed_identity_package_absent": true, "changed_root_identity_refused": true, "existing_destination_refused": true, "original_package_files_unchanged": true, "q01-r2_native_acl_after_sha256": "6d883fe010f0cce1aa27f3f0ef7942d1af18adf7bc59825f0143f659abecb5ee", "q01-r2_native_acl_before_sha256": "6d883fe010f0cce1aa27f3f0ef7942d1af18adf7bc59825f0143f659abecb5ee", "q01-r2_native_acl_snapshot_equal": true, "q02_native_acl_after_sha256": "bf5f539702d64aa7984b7ab3b9313411875a9edd7a147b3d49f8324c29d1b076", "q02_native_acl_before_sha256": "bf5f539702d64aa7984b7ab3b9313411875a9edd7a147b3d49f8324c29d1b076", "q02_native_acl_snapshot_equal": true, "wrong_key_published_root_absent": true, "wrong_key_refused": true}}, "diagnostic-ledger.json": [{"id": "task-root-private-acl", "kind": "setup_failure", "reason": "Initial SID formatting error 1332; corrected in task-root-private-acl-retry."}, {"id": "run-q01", "kind": "observation_failure", "reason": "Initial file census tried to read locked coordinator.lock; corrected census records PermissionError; Q01 r2 succeeded."}, {"id": "list-task-fixture-outputs", "kind": "inspection_failure", "reason": "PowerShell filter typo; corrected by list-task-fixture-outputs-r2."}, {"id": "q03-build-current-fixture", "kind": "builder_failure", "reason": "Goal problem-id mismatch; corrected in q03-build-current-fixture-r2 using a separate root."}, {"id": "run-q03-current", "kind": "shell_failure", "reason": "Nested Windows PowerShell 5 lacked utf8NoBOM; rerun with installed pwsh in run-q03-current-r2."}, {"id": "verify-q03-current-history", "kind": "verifier_failure", "reason": "Initial verifier queried absent resource_effects.state; corrected to body JSON state."}, {"id": "verify-q03-current-history-r2", "kind": "verifier_failure", "reason": "Initial status assertion expected RUNNING; observed valid source QUEUED and corrected to QUEUED -> RECONCILING."}, {"id": "verify-q03-current-history-r3", "kind": "verifier_failure", "reason": "Diagnostic output captured source QUEUED and restored RECONCILING before correcting assertion."}, {"id": "concurrent_writer", "kind": "untested_limit", "reason": "No controlled concurrent business writer point-in-time assertion; idle held lease only."}], "source-helper-overlay-manifest.json": {"source_commit": "4f4023c956f84d65743f39ce77d6c8899a21ada1", "source_tree": "3db13a15cc52b2b0bd75cae3452c66509a9f55c9", "source_edit": false, "helper_and_overlay": {"Invoke-EvidenceCommand.ps1": {"sha256": "7e9eb4a705adc41438fd9813151e5076d7c4fd1e29e9a38a09e97df330a2110b", "bytes": 2674}, "run_case.ps1": {"sha256": "573c39dd1e7c152029d5ce55af013703dd8e01dde94fdeeacef48dfe87567a16", "bytes": 6664}, "census.py": {"sha256": "65f595ed315b208bf5e85bbea40a6d58f7e5648851895d28bc426235fa388154", "bytes": 3164}, "compare_census.py": {"sha256": "81d39f413d3251708ea44748c4677a63e170393936d3362a47579ec79328f8fe", "bytes": 1943}, "verify_restore.py": {"sha256": "cbe6bc0160eb846ee3c0a2b778cea8c50555a98bc34d6d07f202efefe919f79e", "bytes": 3408}, "verify_q03.py": {"sha256": "171123e55baa56ba18e2701d98d48eb96f0d67a506536280a540a903acb44ced", "bytes": 3574}, "negative_summary.py": {"sha256": "ff711d84a86fbe173454dd42fb8cce7c0c893b8454337996cbca2f546bfeb722", "bytes": 1731}, "inspect_q03.py": {"sha256": "5762d7bbda476234e31f6dc5e4e77f9c52b21244b36bbed167f8f28be1f55dc2", "bytes": 2609}, "copy_q03_candidate.ps1": {"sha256": "4c8b23692bf55bed30f710cf8b11e878202